---
title: Roasted Chickpea & Halloumi Salad with Giant Cous Cous
source: Roasting Tin
servings: 2
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
---

Preheat the oven to 180°C fan.

Tip @wholewheat giant cous cous{200%g} and @vegetable stock{450%ml} into a #medium roasting tin{}.

Toss @halloumi{250%g}(cut into 1cm chunks), @chickpeas{1%tin}(drained and rinsed), and @red onion{1}(finely sliced) with @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, then scatter this all over the cous cous.

Transfer the tin to the oven and bake for ~{25%minutes}, until the halloumi is golden brown and the cous cous is cooked through.

Stir through @extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp}, @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, and @spinach{100%g}(roughly chopped), then taste and adjust the seasoning with @salt{} as required.

Divide between lunchboxes and refrigerate until needed.

> Best eaten at room temperature.
